lj1BLfHxl6I;;;We Are Number One (epic funny meme edition super remastered not gay) - LazyTown: The Video Game;;;https://siivagunner.fandom.com/wiki/We%20Are%20Number%20One%20(epic%20funny%20meme%20edition%20super%20remastered%20not%20gay)%20-%20LazyTown%3A%20The%20Video%20Game ;;;   This rip uses several different edits of "We Are Number One" with various sources, each playing after the other:  At the start, it uses "Right In" by Skrillex with "Net" from "We Are Number One" played at 0:01, followed by a bass noise at 0:02. At 0:03, it plays the opening of "We Are Number One" with "Takyon (Death Yon)" pitch-shifted to it. At 0:06, the saxophone is briefly pitch-shifted to "Meet the Flintstones" before it rapidly changes to random notes, followed by "Eh" from "IV. Sweatpants" by Childish Gambino. At 0:09, several sources are arranged and mashed up with "We Are Number One":   Time  Joke  Source   0:09  Gun sounds  Unknown   "S.L.A.B. Freestyle"  Chip tha Ripper   "We Are Number One"  LazyTown   0:13  "What" sample  ???   "Space Jam" (off-beat with "We Are Number One")  Quad City DJs   0:14  Airhorn Sound Effect  N/A   0:19  "Kyoto"  Skrillex  At 0:21, it plays "Death Wish" by Excision ft. Sam King with it pitch-shifted to "We Are Number One", referencing "Death Wish - Excision's Heckin' Epic Safari". At 0:32, a bass noise briefly plays, as the drum beat from "S.L.A.B. Freestyle" is added. At 0:44, it abruptly cuts to "And now for something completely different" from Monty Python, with "different" cut off by Senor Chang's "Ha, Gay!" meme. At 0:46, it plays a off-beat mashup with "Pen-Pineapple-Apple-Pen" and "リサフランク420 / 現代のコンピュー" that is cutoff by "All Is Fair In Love And Brostep" by Skrillex 0:51. At 0:52, several lines from "We Are Number One" are sentenced-mixed to "Pen-Pineapple-Apple-Pen", with "U Guessed It" by OG Maco appearing at 0:56, along with a bass noise, and "Gangnam Style" at 1:01, followed by the Howie Scream. At 1:04, the "Damn son, where'd ya find this?" line by Shadoe Haze plays. At 1:06, "I'll be honest... fellas, it was sounding great. But... I could've used a little more cowbell" from Saturday Night Live plays, with the last word cut off by "GRAND DAD" from GRAND DAD - Vinesauce Joel. At 1:11, it then cuts to a off-beat mashup of "Title Theme & Ending", "Spanish Flea" by Herb Alpert The Tijuana Brass, and "We Are Number One" with it then switching to a on-beat "Spanish Flea" and "We Are Number One" mashup at 1:17, accompanied by airhorns, gun sound effects, and "What" samples. At 1:29, an "Op" from "Gangnam Style" and a laugh track ends the section. At 1:33, several lines are played after each other   Time  Joke  Source   1:30  "Wanna hear the most annoying sound in the world?"  Dumb And Dumber   1:33  "No" (We Are Number One)  LazyTown   1:34  "You're gonna extract him?"  Metal Gear Solid V: The Phantom Pain   1:35  hey peter  At 1:40, an unknown source is used which is abruptly followed by "Don't touch that!" from "We Are Number One". At 1:49, it plays a section of "We Are Number One" right before the chorus, though at a lower pitch. The overall joke is in reference to various edits involving "We Are Number One" at the time that often have high views despite being low effort in many cases and sometimes even gaining money from them. The mix name is in reference to both the rip "Main Theme (super remastered not gay version) - Metal Gear Solid" and "we are number one funny epic meme edition", also by NBGMusic, which features first 44 seconds of the rip;;;NBGMusic
